  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Prefix sum",
  "patterns": [
    "prefix sum",
    "hash map"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "you want the longest subarray summing to k. if you know the running prefix sum at index i, what earlier prefix sum value would you need to have seen for the gap to sum to exactly k?",
    "prefixSum[i] - k - if that value was seen at some earlier index j, the subarray from j+1 to i sums to k",
    "keep a hash map from prefix sum value to the EARLIEST index it occurred at (seed sum 0 at index -1, for subarrays starting from index 0)",
    "at each index, look up prefixSum[i] - k in the map; if found at index j, the length i - j is a candidate for the longest answer - only insert a NEW sum into the map if it hasn't been seen before, to preserve earliest indices"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "overwriting an existing prefix sum's stored index with a later one, which shortens the subarray you'd find",
    "forgetting to seed prefix sum 0 at index -1",
    "confusing this with 'count subarrays summing to k' (which just counts occurrences) instead of tracking the longest length, which needs first-occurrence indices"
  ],
